      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #2, 2026-08-06): f¨ on an
      ⍝ empty nested array whose (disclosed) prototype item has more
      ⍝ than one element used to build a result with uninitialized
      ⍝ Cells (aborts via Cell::init_other()'s assert, or dispatches a
      ⍝ garbage vtable call with asserts off). ScalarFunction.cc's
      ⍝ do_eval_fill_B() only ever wrote cell 0 of the fill result,
      ⍝ regardless of how many cells the (possibly non-scalar)
      ⍝ prototype item actually needed.
      ⍝
      Z1←+¨ 0⍴⊂⍳3
      ⍴⍴Z1
1
      ⍴Z1
0

      Z2←-¨ 0⍴⊂⍳3
      ⍴Z2
0

      ⍝ previously-working single-element-prototype case: still correct
      ⍝
      Z3←+¨0⍴⊂1
      ⍴Z3
0

      ⍝ Bugs28 #35 regression: (F⍤y)¨B (and other derived functions
      ⍝ whose operand is a defined/⎕FX'd function) with an empty B
      ⍝ returned a non-empty scalar/vector instead of an empty array.
      ⍝ Root cause: the empty-argument fill-function branch called
      ⍝ LO->eval_B(*first_B) whenever LO wasn't itself is_defined(),
      ⍝ and returned that call's result token unchanged when its class
      ⍝ wasn't TC_VALUE. For a derived LO wrapping a defined function,
      ⍝ eval_B() pushes a real SI frame and returns TOK_SI_PUSHED, so
      ⍝ the *result of running that frame* silently became the result
      ⍝ of the whole ¨ expression. Fixed in Bif_OPER1_EACH.cc by
      ⍝ treating LO->may_push_SI() the same as LO->is_defined() (both
      ⍝ mean: the fill function is the identity function, i.e. B
      ⍝ itself) -- except for ⎕EC, which also may_push_SI() but has
      ⍝ its own dedicated fabricated fill value.
      ⍝
      ⎕FX 'Z←ZZ35F B' 'Z←B+1'
ZZ35F

      Z←(ZZ35F⍤1)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      Z←(ZZ35F⍤1)¨0⍴⊂1 2 3 ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴(⊂3⍴0 0 0)

      Z←(ZZ35F⍤0)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      Z←(ZZ35F¨)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      Z←({⍵+1}⍤1)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      Z←({⍵+1}¨)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      Z←(ZZ35F⍣2)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      ⎕FX 'Z←ZZ35G LO' 'Z←LO+1'
ZZ35G

      Z←(ZZ35G/)¨⍬ ⋄ 2 ⎕TF 'Z'
Z←0⍴0

      )ERASE ZZ35F ZZ35G
